; Reads alone do not make a program confluent.  The row (row $x) is still
; open: reading it as (row a) decides $x = a, and reading it as (row b)
; decides $x = b.  Even with a set store, the two firings end in two outcomes;
; a single fixpoint needs ground rows that no firing refines.
(step one)
(store set)
(row $x)
(rule pick-a (read (row a)) (make (chosen a)))
(rule pick-b (read (row b)) (make (chosen b)))
